# Purpose: Add misc/wcstold.c to mingw32_arm_src so the public wcstold symbol
#          is compiled for thumb/aarch64-windows-gnu, not just x86/x86_64.
#          misc/mingw_wcstold.c (the __mingw_wcstold implementation) is already
#          compiled unconditionally for all arches via mingw32_generic_src, but
#          misc/wcstold.c (the thin wrapper that exports the public `wcstold`
#          symbol) is upstream-gated to mingw32_x86_src (x86/x86_64 only). This
#          leaves aarch64-windows-gnu with an implementation but no exported
#          entry point, so linking libc++ (libcxx/src/string.cpp:283 calls
#          std::__1::stold -> wcstold) fails with:
#            lld-link: error: undefined symbol: wcstold
# Affects: src/libs/mingw.zig
# Prerequisite: patches/non_unix/mingw-arm64-stubs.patch (applies immediately
#          before this one in recipe.yaml; both patch the same file region).
# Upstream: TBD
# drop-when: zig upstream adds misc/wcstold.c to mingw32_arm_src (or otherwise
#            compiles it for thumb/aarch64 targets)
# Last-verified: 2026-08-11

From: zig-feedstock
Subject: [PATCH] mingw: add misc/wcstold.c to mingw32_arm_src for aarch64-windows-gnu

The public wcstold wrapper is x86-gated upstream while its __mingw_wcstold
implementation is generic, so aarch64-windows-gnu links fail on the public
wcstold symbol. Adding misc/wcstold.c to mingw32_arm_src (compiled for both
thumb and aarch64) resolves the undefined symbol without touching the
generic __mingw_wcstold implementation or any x86 source list.

drop-when: zig upstream adds misc/wcstold.c to mingw32_arm_src

--- a/src/libs/mingw.zig
+++ b/src/libs/mingw.zig
@@ -915,2 +915,3 @@
     "math" ++ path.sep_str ++ "arm-common" ++ path.sep_str ++ "ldexpl.c",
+    "misc" ++ path.sep_str ++ "wcstold.c",
 };
